-- title:
--   Proposition 3.16 — the key error bound for the general case
-- statement:
--   Let Assumptions 2.17 and 2.19 hold, let $\boldsymbol\alpha^N$ be a Nash equilibrium of the $N$-player game for each $N$ (state process $\mathbf X^N$), and let $(m,\alpha)$ be a MFE (state process $X$). Let $(X,Y,Z,Z^0)$ be a solution of (3.6) with $\alpha_t=\hat\alpha(X_t,Y_t,Z_t,Z^0_t,m_t)$, and let $(X^i,Y^i,Z^i,Z^{i,0})$ and $\alpha^i$ be conditionally independent copies. Then there are $N_0\in\mathbb N$ and $C>0$ such that for each $N\ge N_0$,
--   $$\sum_{i=1}^N\mathbb E\Big[\sup_{0\le t\le T}|X^{N,i}_t-X^i_t|^2\Big]\le C\,\mathbb E\Big[\int_0^T\sum_i\big(|E^{b,i}_t|^2+|E^{\sigma,i}_t|^2+|E^{\sigma^0,i}_t|^2+|E^{L,i}_t|^2\big)dt+\sum_i|E^{G,i}|^2\Big].$$
--   If in addition $\hat\alpha$ is Lipschitz and, for fixed $(x,y,z,z^0)$, $m\mapsto\hat\alpha(x,y,z,z^0,m)$ has first and second Lions derivatives which are bounded and Lipschitz uniformly in $(x,y,z,z^0)$, then
--   $$\sum_{i=1}^N\mathbb E\Big[\int_0^T|\alpha^{N,i}_t-\alpha^i_t|^2dt\Big]\le\frac CN+C\,\mathbb E\Big[\int_0^T\sum_i\big(|E^{b,i}_t|^2+|E^{\sigma,i}_t|^2+|E^{\sigma^0,i}_t|^2+|E^{L,i}_t|^2\big)dt+\sum_i|E^{G,i}|^2\Big].$$
--   The error terms are those of the item `IsSol_3_6`. They compare the copies' empirical measure with the conditional law, which Lemma 3.13 bounds by $C/N$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: the canonical spaces $\Omega^N=(\mathbb R^n)^N\times\mathcal C^{N+1}$ with product measure, embedded in one another (pp.9–10) → one probability space carrying $\xi^1,\xi^2,\dots$ (law $m_0$), $W^0$ and $W^1,W^2,\dots$, mutually independent, Brownian paths continuous (`Setup`); reason: the canonical product space is an instance, so the statement specializes to the paper's
--   - generalization: $d,k,n\in\mathbb N=\{1,2,\dots\}$ → any $n,k,d\ge 0$; reason: the source's dimensions are instances
--   - encoding: augmented filtrations $\mathbb F^N$, $\mathbb F^0$ → the raw filtrations generated by $\xi^1,\dots,\xi^N,W^0,\dots,W^N$ and by $W^0$; reason: every process progressive for the augmented filtration has a raw-progressive version ([41, Prop. 1.2.1], cited p.10); controls and states enter only up to versions
--   - encoding: continuous processes → processes with almost surely continuous paths on $[0,T]$; reason: on a general probability space continuity holds outside a null set; suprema and integrals do not see null sets
--   - encoding: players $i\in\{1,\dots,N\}$ → players `i : Fin N`, player $i$ of the paper is index $i-1$; reason: relabelling
--   - encoding: $\mathbb R^{n\times d}$ with the Frobenius norm and $A\cdot B=\mathrm{tr}(A^\top B)$ → `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n × Fin d)`; reason: same norm and inner product
--   - encoding: a Nash equilibrium $\boldsymbol\alpha^N$ and "the state process corresponding to $\boldsymbol\alpha^N$" → `IsNashN`: admissible $\boldsymbol\alpha^N$, its state process $\mathbf X^N$ solving (2.3), compared against every admissible deviation and every state process of the deviation; reason: strong solutions are unique under Lipschitz data, so "every" and "the" agree
--   - encoding: $J^{N,i}$, $J_m$ real valued (footnote 1, p.12) → the costs of the equilibrium are finite, and only deviations with finite (integrable) cost are compared; reason: under the paper's assumptions every cost is finite, so the compared sets coincide
--   - encoding: $m_t=\mathcal L(X_t\mid\mathcal F^0_t)$ → $\omega\mapsto m_t(\omega)(A)$ is a.s. equal to $\mathbb P[X_t\in A\mid\mathcal F^0_t]$ for every Borel $A$ (`IsCondLaw`); $\mathbb F^0$-adaptedness of $m$ through the evaluation maps; reason: this is the definition of a version of the conditional law
--   - encoding: the copies $X^i_t=\widetilde X_t(\xi^i,W^0_{[0,t]},W^i_{[0,t]})$ of Definition 2.2 built from the representation of Lemma 2.1 → copies built from any representation (`ContRep` for $X$: copies adapted with a.s. continuous paths; `ProgRep` for $\alpha$: copies progressive); reason: Lemma 2.1 provides one, and two representations give a.s. equal copies at each $t$
--   - encoding: §2.3: Fréchet differentiability of the lift $\xi\mapsto U(x,\mathcal L(\xi))$ on $\mathbb L^2(\Omega)$, with continuous $D_mU$ → the published `DisplMonoMFG.WellPosed.HasLDeriv` (first-order expansion uniform over the joint laws of $(\xi,\eta)$ with $\mathcal L(\xi)=m$), plus joint continuity; versions of $D_m$ as data (`Derivs`); reason: on an atomless space the two notions coincide; a Lions derivative is determined only $m$-a.e., and every statement evaluates it on the support
--   - encoding: "Lipschitz in all arguments", "bounded", "$C^1$" for maps on $\mathbb R^p\times\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R^n)$ → `LipXM`, `BddXM`, `IsC1` with $\mathcal W_2$ in the measure and the max-norm on the product of the other arguments; reason: equivalent norms give the same notions up to the (existential) constants
--   - encoding: "for any square-integrable random variables" in (1.6), (2.16), (2.19) → for every coupling $\pi$ with finite second moments, the laws being the marginals of $\pi$, whenever the integrand is integrable; reason: random variables enter only through their joint law, and every coupling is a joint law on an atomless space
--   - encoding: $\hat\alpha$, the unique minimizer of (3.1) → `alphaHat`: a minimizer chosen by `Classical.choose`, `0` if none exists; reason: the minimizer exists and is unique under Assumptions 2.5, 2.12 and 2.19 (p.19)
--   - encoding: $D_yH$, $D_zH$, $D_{z^0}H$, $D_xH$ in the FBSDEs (3.2), (3.6) → their minimizer form $b(x,\hat\alpha,m)$, $\sigma(x,\hat\alpha,m)$, $\sigma^0(x,\hat\alpha,m)$, $D_x[b\cdot y+\sigma\cdot z+\sigma^0\cdot z^0](x,\hat\alpha,m)+D_xL(x,\hat\alpha,m)$; reason: equal wherever $H$ is differentiable ($H\le$ the minimized function, with equality at $\hat\alpha$), in particular under Assumption 2.17; it is the form of (3.4), (3.5), (3.9), (3.10) in the other two cases
--   - encoding: backward equations with terminal condition → forward Itô form from the random initial value together with the terminal condition (`IsItoProc` + a.s. terminal value); reason: the integral form of a BSDE
--   - encoding: $\mathbb E[\sup_t|\cdot|^2]$, $\mathbb E\int_0^T|\cdot|^2dt$ → lower Lebesgue integrals in $[0,\infty]$, bound $\mathrm{ofReal}(C/N)$; reason: same value; an infinite left side violates the bound in both
--   - reading: "bounded and Lipschitz in $m$, uniformly in $(x,y,z,z^0)$" (Assumption 2.20, Theorem 2.23 (2)) → one bound and one $\mathcal W_2$-Lipschitz constant in $m$, valid for all other arguments including the points $p,q$ (`TwoLionsUnif`); reason: the page asks Lipschitz continuity in $m$ uniformly in the remaining arguments
--   - reading: $E^{f,i}$ in the bound, and $D_xG(X^i_T,\bar m^N_t)$ in $E^{G,i}$ → $E^{L,i}$, and $D_xG(X^i_T,\bar m^N_T)$; reason: $E^{L,i}$ is the only running-cost error defined; $E^{G,i}$ is a terminal error
--   - reading: $D_{mm}\hat\alpha=D_m[\hat\alpha(x,y,z,z^0,\cdot)](m,p,q)$ (p.35) → the second Lions derivative $D_{mm}\hat\alpha$; reason: Theorem 2.23 (p.18) states the same condition with $D_{mm}$
--   - reading: the solution $(X,Y,Z,Z^0)$ of (3.6) and its copies (implicit on p.34; Step 1 takes one from Lemma 3.5) → every solution of (3.6) with $\alpha=\hat\alpha(X,Y,Z,Z^0,m)$ $dt\otimes d\mathbb P$-a.e., and every representation of its components; reason: the universal reading is the stronger statement
--   - encoding: $\bar m_t=\mathcal L(X^i_t\mid\mathcal F^0_t)$ → $m_t$; reason: every copy has the conditional law $m_t$ of $X_t$ (Lemma 2.1 and (2.9))
--   - encoding: "Let $\boldsymbol\alpha^N$ be a Nash equilibrium" with a conclusion "for each $N\ge N_0$" → a family $(\boldsymbol\alpha^N)_{N\ge1}$ of Nash equilibria, with $N_0$ and $C$ chosen before $N$; reason: the conclusion ranges over $N$
--   - encoding: one pair $(N_0,C)$ for both conclusions → a pair for each conclusion; reason: taking the larger of each gives a common pair
-- source:
--   Jackson & Tangpi, Quantitative Convergence for Displacement Monotone Mean Field Games with Controlled Volatility, arXiv:2304.04543v2, Proposition 3.16 and Step 1 of its proof, pp.34–35

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CtrlVolMFG_IsSol_3_6

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory
open scoped ENNReal NNReal

namespace CtrlVolMFG

/-- Proposition 3.16 (Jackson & Tangpi, arXiv:2304.04543v2, pp.34–35): let Assumptions 2.17 and
2.19 hold, let `αᴺ` be a Nash equilibrium of the `N`-player game for each `N` (state process
`Xᴺ`), and let `(m, α)` be a MFE (state process `X`). Let `(X, Y, Z, Z⁰)` be a solution of (3.6)
with `α_t = α̂(X_t, Y_t, Z_t, Z⁰_t, m_t)` `dt × dℙ`-a.e. (it exists by Lemma 3.5), and let
`(Xⁱ, Yⁱ, Zⁱ, Z^{i,0})`, `αⁱ` be its conditionally independent copies and those of `α`. Then there
are `N₀`, `C > 0` such that for each `N ≥ N₀`,
`∑ᵢ 𝔼[sup_{0≤t≤T}|X^{N,i}_t − Xⁱ_t|²] ≤ C 𝔼[∫₀ᵀ ∑ᵢ(|E^{b,i}_t|² + |E^{σ,i}_t|² + |E^{σ⁰,i}_t|² +
|E^{L,i}_t|²)dt + ∑ᵢ|E^{G,i}|²]` (`errSum`). If in addition `α̂` is Lipschitz and has bounded,
Lipschitz first and second Lions derivatives uniformly in `(x, y, z, z⁰)` (`AlphaHatReg`), then
`∑ᵢ 𝔼∫₀ᵀ|α^{N,i}_t − αⁱ_t|²dt ≤ C/N + C 𝔼[…]` with the same expectation.

**Formalization Note** The statement holds for every such solution of (3.6). The page's `E^{f,i}`
is `E^{L,i}`, and the `D_xG(Xⁱ_T, m̄ᴺ_t)` term of `E^{G,i}` is read at `T`; `D_mmα̂` is the second
Lions derivative (the page writes `D_m`, compare p.18). -/
theorem proposition_3_16 {n k d : ℕ} {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (S : Setup n d Ω)
    (D : Data n k d) (V : Derivs n k d) (T : ℝ≥0) (hT : 0 < T)
    (h17 : Assumption_2_17 D V) (h19 : Assumption_2_19 D)
    (αN : ∀ N : ℕ, Fin N → ℝ≥0 → Ω → Rn k) (XN : ∀ N : ℕ, Fin N → ℝ≥0 → Ω → Rn n)
    (hNash : ∀ N, 0 < N → IsNashN S D T N (αN N) (XN N))
    (m : ℝ≥0 → Ω → P2 n) (α : ℝ≥0 → Ω → Rn k) (X : ℝ≥0 → Ω → Rn n) (hMFE : IsMFE S D T m α X)
    (Y : ℝ≥0 → Ω → Rn n) (Z Z0 : ℝ≥0 → Ω → Mat n d) (hsol : IsSol_3_6 S D T m X Y Z Z0)
    (hα : EqDtDP S.P T α (fun t ω => D.alphaHat (X t ω) (Y t ω) (Z t ω) (Z0 t ω) (m t ω)))
    (RX : ContRep S T X) (RY : ContRep S T Y) (RZ : ProgRep S T Z) (RZ0 : ProgRep S T Z0)
    (Rα : ProgRep S T α) :
    (∃ N0 : ℕ, ∃ C > 0, ∀ N ≥ N0, 0 < N →
      ∑ i : Fin N, ∫⁻ ω, ⨆ t ∈ Set.Icc 0 T, ‖XN N i t ω - RX.copy i t ω‖ₑ ^ 2 ∂S.P ≤
        ENNReal.ofReal C *
          errSum S D V N T m RX.copy RY.copy RZ.copy RZ0.copy) ∧
    (AlphaHatReg D → ∃ N0 : ℕ, ∃ C > 0, ∀ N ≥ N0, 0 < N →
      ∑ i : Fin N, ∫⁻ ω, ∫⁻ s in Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) T,
          ‖αN N i s.toNNReal ω - Rα.copy i s.toNNReal ω‖ₑ ^ 2 ∂volume ∂S.P ≤
        ENNReal.ofReal (C / N) + ENNReal.ofReal C *
          errSum S D V N T m RX.copy RY.copy RZ.copy RZ0.copy) := by sorry

end CtrlVolMFG
